
PROGRAM 57: Smart Canteen Order and Stock Management

AIM
To calculate an order cost and update canteen stock.

FEATURES
- Stores item prices and stock.
- Checks available stock.
- Calculates the bill and updates stock.

PROGRAM
stock = {"Sandwich": 10, "Juice": 8}
price = {"Sandwich": 40, "Juice": 25}

item = "Sandwich"
quantity = 2

if quantity <= stock[item]:
    bill = quantity * price[item]
    stock[item] -= quantity
    print("Item:", item)
    print("Bill amount:", bill)
    print("Stock left:", stock[item])
else:
    print("Not enough stock")

EXPLANATION
The program checks whether enough stock is available. If it is, the bill is calculated and stock is reduced.

SAMPLE INPUT / DATA
The sample item and quantity are set in the program.

EXPECTED OUTPUT
Item: Sandwich
Bill amount: 80
Stock left: 8

ACTUAL OUTPUT
Same as the expected output when the program is run with the sample input/data above.

RESULT
Thus, the canteen order is billed and stock is updated successfully.
